Before publication, only the private draft can contain partial work; the revision test and publication cannot be separated by another editor's commit. Returning an error must dispose of temporary guest roots and the draft. A proposal count bounds only the number of operations, not their size or the cost of copying the document. Bounded strings and structural sharing can reduce those other costs without giving the guest direct access to the published data.
